# App flexibility (non-negotiable)

one_request is a toolkit, not a locked pipeline. The Flutter app that depends on it must be able to turn off, skip, or replace every feature from `main` / its own API setup.

## Keep these knobs

- `configure(...)` — every field optional; omit = leave unchanged
- Overlays: `enableLoader` / `enableErrorOverlay` / `enableSuccessOverlay`, plus per-request `loader` / `resultOverlay`
- Logging: off by default; `setErrorLoggerEnabled` / `setResponseLoggerEnabled`
- Errors: `setErrorHandler` (additive), `clearErrorHandler()`, `resetErrorHandler()`
- Auth: `setAuth` is optional; `clearAuth()` removes it; apps may still pass headers / interceptors
- Loading UI: `loadingconfig` / `wrap` / `initLoading` are optional. Do not auto-theme EasyLoading from `configure()`
- API style: keep both `send<T>()` (Either) and `request<T>()` (throws). Do not delete Either
- Per-request: headers, interceptors, timeout, retries, cache, cancel token, `innerData` / `unwrap`
- WebSocket: `OneRequest.socket(...)` is opt-in (nothing connects until called). Each call is a new `OneSocket` on any host (`wss://…` or `baseUrl:`). `enableWebSocket: false` hard-disables it. `autoReconnect` defaults off.
- Multiple services: `OneRequest(baseUrl: …)` per host; `configure(baseUrl:)` is only the default for relative paths. Absolute `http(s)` / `ws(s)` URLs are never prefixed.
- Connectivity: off until `setConnectivity()` / `configure(enableConnectivity: true)`. UI is snackbar by default, or `banner` / `popover` / `none` / custom `builder`. `clearConnectivity()` turns it off.

## When adding features

- Default to **off** or **overridable**. Never require a new call in the consuming app.
- Do not remove or hard-code over an existing app callback (error handler, token readers, overlay builders).
- Helpers (`setAuth`, `wrap`, `RestErrorParser`) are shortcuts, not the only path.
